    "sentence_translations": [
      "Ben’s Diary – I Will Make A Call For You",
      "",
      "2018-09-16 Heavy Rain",
      "",
      "Today, Lili said: “Ben, you speak Chinese really well! I will make a call for you!”",
      "",
      "“Make a call? Make a phone call? Lili is going to call me?”",
      "",
      "I was really happy and kept waiting for Lili’s call.",
      "However, even after waiting for a long time, Lili still didn’t call me.",
      "",
      "I then called Lili and asked her why she said she would “make a call”, but never called me on the phone.",
      "",
      "Lili told me that “make a call” doesn’t mean to “make a phone call”.",
      "“Make a call” is a catchphrase.",
      "Nowadays in Chinese, “I make a call for you” means “I cheer for you” or “I like what you’re doing”.",
      "",
      "It turns out Lili wasn’t going to call me.",
      "However, Lili said that I speak Chinese very well, so I’m still happy.",
      ""
    ]
  }
